{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 7 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 7 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nVanya has a scales for weighing loads and weights of masses w0,\u2009w1,\u2009w2,\u2009...,\u2009w100 grams where w is some integer not less than 2 (exactly one weight of each nominal value). Vanya wonders whether he can weight an item with mass m using the given weights, if the weights can be put on both pans of the scales. Formally speaking, your task is to determine whether it is possible to place an item of mass m and some weights on the left pan of the scales, and some weights on the right pan of the scales so that the pans of the scales were in balance.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 7 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class CodeForce308C {\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] tokens = in.readLine().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        long w = Long.parseLong(tokens[0]);\n        long m = Long.parseLong(tokens[1]);\n        \n        if (w == 2) {\n            System.out.println(\"YES\");\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        List<Long> combination = new ArrayList<>();\n        combination.add(0L);\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i <= 100; i++) {\n            long power = 1;\n            if (i > 0) {\n                try {\n                    power = Math.multiplyExact(combination.get(combination.size() - 1) / (i > 1 ? (long) Math.pow(w, i - 1) : 1L), w);\n                } catch (ArithmeticException | IndexOutOfBoundsException e) {\n                    break;\n                }\n            } else {\n                power = 1;\n            }\n            \n            if (power > (long) 2 * Integer.MAX_VALUE) {\n                break;\n            }\n            \n            int currentSize = combination.size();\n            for (int j = 0; j < currentSize; j++) {\n                long sum = combination.get(j) + power;\n                if (sum <= (long) 2 * Integer.MAX_VALUE) {\n                    combination.add(sum);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        Collections.sort(combination);\n        \n        if (Collections.binarySearch(combination, m) >= 0) {\n            System.out.println(\"YES\");\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        for (Long element : combination) {\n            if (element + m <= (long) 2 * Integer.MAX_VALUE && \n                Collections.binarySearch(combination, element + m) >= 0) {\n                System.out.println(\"YES\");\n                return;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(\"NO\");\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class CodeForce308C {\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] tokens = in.readLine().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        long w = Long.parseLong(tokens[0]);\n        long m = Long.parseLong(tokens[1]);\n        \n        // Special case for w=2: always possible\n        if (w == 2) {\n            System.out.println(\"YES\");\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        // Generate all possible combinations of weights on left pan\n        // Each weight can be: not used, on left pan, or on right pan\n        // So we're looking for: m + sum(left_weights) = sum(right_weights)\n        // Which means: m = sum(right_weights) - sum(left_weights)\n        // This is equivalent to representing m in balanced ternary-like system\n        \n        // We'll generate all possible values of (sum of some weights) - (sum of some other weights)\n        // which equals sum(weight_i * coefficient_i) where coefficient_i \u2208 {-1, 0, 1}\n        \n        Set<Long> possibleValues = new HashSet<>();\n        possibleValues.add(0L);\n        \n        long power = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= 100; i++) {\n            Set<Long> newValues = new HashSet<>();\n            \n            for (Long val : possibleValues) {\n                // Three choices: don't use this weight, put on left pan, put on right pan\n                // If on left pan: contributes +power to the difference (right - left)\n                // If on right pan: contributes -power to the difference (right - left)\n                // If not used: contributes 0\n                newValues.add(val);           // not used\n                newValues.add(val + power);   // on left pan (makes left heavier, so right-left decreases by power, but we track right-left)\n                newValues.add(val - power);   // on right pan (makes right heavier, so right-left increases by power)\n            }\n            \n            possibleValues = newValues;\n            \n            // Check for overflow\n            if (power > (long) 1e15) {\n                break;\n            }\n            \n            // Next power\n            try {\n                power = Math.multiplyExact(power, w);\n            } catch (ArithmeticException e) {\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        if (possibleValues.contains(m)) {\n            System.out.println(\"YES\");\n        } else {\n            System.out.println(\"NO\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.576278118089249e-07, -5.6265202147187665e-05, -2.145764938177308e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.890059739816934e-05, -3.1470757676288486e-05, -6.318072337307967e-06, -7.271740287251305e-06, -4.410734163684538e-06, -3.814689989667386e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.950943836476654e-05, -5.364403477869928e-06, -8.583032467868179e-06, -0.00040558696491643786, -0.0003137096355203539, -5.960462772236497e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.861018856492592e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.012510748580098152, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -6.318072337307967e-06, -1.1324817933200393e-05, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -5.364403477869928e-06, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -6.079655122448457e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.00015317220822907984, -1.9788545614574105e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.437280717364047e-06, -1.0251946150674485e-05, -1.311301275563892e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.125986263010418e-06, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -1.9192511899746023e-05, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -0.0003232433518860489, -3.302042750874534e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -3.2186455882765586e-06, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.811964830267243e-05, -2.2411095415009186e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.4638240878121e-06, -2.4318398573086597e-05, -6.079655122448457e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.4424220353248529e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -5.602820692729438e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.390948667307384e-06, -3.576278118089